## Tagged by tda2d
## ZDBsubject(Calculus - multivariable)
## ZDBchapter(Differentiation of multivariable functions)
## ZDBsection(Extreme values and optimization)
## Date(6/3/2002)
## Level(4)
## TitleText1('Calculus: Early Transcendentals')
## AuthorText1('Stewart')
## EditionText1('6')
## Section1('14.7')
## Problem1('2')
## TitleText2('Calculus: Early Transcendentals')
## AuthorText2('Rogawski')
## EditionText2('1')
## Section2('14.7')
## Problem2('2')



DOCUMENT();		# This should be the first executable line in the problem.

loadMacros("PG.pl",      
           "PGbasicmacros.pl",
           "PGchoicemacros.pl",      
           "PGanswermacros.pl",
           "PGauxiliaryFunctions.pl"     
          );      

TEXT(beginproblem());
$showPartialCorrectAnswers = 1;

$a = random(1, 5, 1);
$b = random(1, 5, 1);
$c = random(1, 5, 1);
$d = 2*$a;
$e = 2*$b;

BEGIN_TEXT
Soit la fonction \( f(x, y) = x^{2} + y^{2} - $d x - $e y + $c \).
$PAR
Trouvez les points critiques de \(f\) sur \(\mathbb{R}^{2}\) et calculez la valeur de \(f\) en chacun.
$PAR
$BBOLD (a) $EBOLD
Combien de points critiques \( f \) admet-elle sur \( \mathbb{R}^{2} \) ?
$PAR
\(\ \ \ \) \{ ans_rule(10) \}
$PAR
$BBOLD (b) $EBOLD
Coordonnées du point critique :
\( \displaystyle (x_0,\, y_0) = \Big( \)\{ ans_rule(10) \}\(,\ \)\{ ans_rule(10) \}\( \Big) \)
$PAR
$BBOLD (c) $EBOLD
Valeur de \(f\) en ce point critique :
$PAR
\(\ \ \ f(x_0, y_0) = \) \{ ans_rule(10) \}
END_TEXT

ANS(num_cmp(1));
ANS(num_cmp($a));
ANS(num_cmp($b));
ANS(num_cmp("$c - $a**2 - $b**2"));

ENDDOCUMENT();		# This should be the last executable line in the problem.
